<title>DUBAI: UAE destroys pirated tapes in copyright crackdown.</title>
<headline>UAE destroys pirated tapes in copyright crackdown.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates has destroyed thousands of pirated audio and video cassettes in a crackdown on copyright violations, newspapers said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said the Ministry of Information and Culture destroyed 57,000 audio tapes, 31,000 video tapes and 1,916 compact discs earlier this week.</p>
<p>Copyright laws were introduced in the UAE in 1992.</p>
<p>The Gulf state has in recent years stepped up its drive to enforce the law and authorities regularly raid shops and companies suspected of selling pirated goods.</p>
</text>
